From 8194509f2af2ef39ed9f5d0cd6a7ab1e7f56a5b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 15:16:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ArtCraft: a title of its own (PPSA99278, /data/artcraft)
 beside MihawkOS

ArtCraft installs next to MihawkOS and shares nothing with it. MihawkOS
is PPSA99170 and keeps its Wine runtime, prefixes, library, logs, setup
record, update staging, shared sections, payload child and root daemon
log under /data/ps5proton. A title with either value would replace it or
share all of that with it. ArtCraft's runtime is not MihawkOS's: its
Windows user, Start menu and wallpaper differ.

So the title, the runtime and the root daemon's log, and the PC tools
that install and test them (console-setup.py, deploy-wine.py,
pack-runtime.py, package-install.py, sign-release.py, the gate's runners)
with their tests, all name PPSA99278 and /data/artcraft. That includes
Z:\data\artcraft in every escaping the probes use. param.json carries
conceptId 99278 and contentId UP9000-PPSA99278_00-ARTCRAFT00000000. The
service helper now loads gpu-client.prx from ArtCraft's own folder, not
MihawkOS's. The publication check counts PPSA99278 as the title's own.

MihawkOS's documents (*.md) and the records of its console runs
(evidence/, docs/history/) are unchanged: they describe MihawkOS.

Made by PS5-ARTCRAFT's artcraft_ps5/identity.py. It refuses to run if
the tree names an update feed or a release key, since ArtCraft would
then offer MihawkOS's releases as its own updates. Every one of the 102
changed files reverses byte for byte to its committed text when the two
values are swapped back, so nothing else changed.

Proven on the host: the profile, launch, prefix, setup and detailed-logs
tests, as root and as an unprivileged user; the logo, icon and package
tests; all 148 Python tests with the same outcome as before; and
proton_launch.cpp, proton_install.cpp and proton_update.cpp compiling
in the host-reference configuration as PPSA99278.
